If you want to know, here is the source info: AC is of type schar.
Now schar is normally typedef'ed to signed char - and thus can't go
below -127. But it must not be - in fact the cource code remarks, that 
some compilers can't handle that, and in such cases it should be
short int (with appropriate range). Thus, while it is true that in
your nethack (and probably 99% others as well) the AC can't go below -127,
it is not generally so...

